10
00:54:42,352 --> 00:54:48,352
Griff the Invisible is a 2010 Australian romantic superhero
comedy-drama film written and directed by Leon Ford.

11
01:00:10,588 --> 01:00:16,588
Its storyline centres on a socially awkward office worker bullied by his workmates during the daytime and turning
himself at nighttime into a superhero who roams the streets of his neighbourhood and protects the innocent.

12
01:05:38,823 --> 01:05:44,823
Griff the Invisible had its world premiere at the 2010 Toronto International Film Festival (TIFF),
where it was well received by audiences "who seemed charmed by this offbeat tale".

13
01:11:07,058 --> 01:11:13,058
It also screened at the 2011 Berlin International Film Festival in February 2011 in the
"generation" sidebar where it was well received by a predominantly teenage crowd.

14
01:16:35,294 --> 01:16:41,294
The film won the AACTA award for Best Original Screenplay.

15
01:22:03,529 --> 01:22:09,529
The film explores themes of superhero, bullying, love, loneliness, scientist.

16
01:27:31,764 --> 01:27:37,764
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
